formulations.statement:
f(z) := Σ_{t≥0} c(t)·z^t is not a rational function: there are no polynomials P, Q with Q ≠ 0 and Q·f = P over ℚ (equivalently over ℂ). Equivalently, c satisfies no eventual linear recurrence Σ_{i≤d} a_i·c(n+i) = 0 (for n ≥ N) with constant coefficients not all zero.
Over 𝔽₂ the following are also equivalent:
- f ∉ 𝔽₂(z);
- c is not the output of any LFSR;
- the linear complexity L(n) of c(0..n−1) is unbounded;
- the continued fraction of Σ c(t)·X^{-t-1} in 𝔽₂((1/X)) is infinite.

