formulations.statement:
For no k ≥ 2 is c k-automatic. Two equivalent forms:
- by Adamczewski–Bell–Smertnig 2023, f(z) satisfies no Mahler equation Σ_{i≤d} P_i(z)·f(z^{k^i}) = 0 with polynomials P_i not all zero;
- for prime k, by Christol, f is transcendental over 𝔽_k(z).

Every binary word w of length k occurs in c with asymptotic frequency 2^{-k}. Equivalent forms:
- (2^t·x₂ mod 1)_t is uniformly distributed (Wall 1949);
- x₂ is simply normal to base 2^k for every k (Pillai 1940).

