2. Because of Jen's theorem, no other column, including the white-seed column -1, can be proved equivalent to Problem 1 without solving it.
3. Diagonals are periodic (the solved analogue); lines of other slopes are open analogues.
4. The project's CQ01 is exactly the period-2 case of the finite-configuration problem, from time 0. Q01 already covers all left-finite rows. All project reductions are uniform over finite rows, so each is at least as strong as the finite-configuration case for its period.

